REQ-PRODUCTION-002,PARTIAL,566,567,b637d970225d18be49edeb86e35348198461d055,"PR #567 delivers the first bounded REQ-PRODUCTION-002 Phase-2 slice: src/simulation/productionPlanning.ts defines deterministic ProductionPlan/LaborDemandPlan construction for ACTIVE units, derives effective capacity from live installedCapital plus explicit bounded physical productivity evidence, applies the canonical adaptive-utilization formula, reserves mandatory cash and operating liquidity then affordable gross payroll before INPUT procurement, and emits stable validated BUY/INPUT MarketIntents whose total maxSpend is bounded by the remaining opening home-currency procurement envelope. The Phase-2 handler commits every emitted INPUT BUY maxSpend through the existing TickContext budget ledger under ProductionPlan.planId and fails closed when a duplicate/overcommit would exceed procurementCashEnvelope. The planning evidence boundary exposes only opening/prior-close inputs; src/simulation/productionPlanning.test.ts includes sensitive regressions proving same-tick sale transactions/market outputs cannot increase Phase-2 financing, shuffled recipe/price insertion order normalizes identically, non-ACTIVE units have zero normal production/labor demand, invalid/non-finite evidence fails fast, and `commits Phase-2 INPUT maxSpend to the plan envelope and rejects duplicate overcommit` proves the ledger commitment equals the submitted maxSpend total and duplicate resubmission is rejected. Repair head 700073a777d2e9ca32c7e826f5d4dc29612dacf3 passed CI #1172 / Actions run 35365749979: TypeScript typecheck/tests/build, retained .NET build/test, policy-guard and mergeability. This row is deliberately PARTIAL: Handoff/05 section 15 cadence-based INVESTMENT budget/BUY intents remain a separate REQ-PRODUCTION-002 slice; investmentIntentIds stays empty here. Phase-3 labor allocation, Phase-5 execution/output sale, Phase-12 investment conversion/depreciation, lifecycle transitions and M5+ are not claimed."
