REQ-PRODUCTION-002,IMPLEMENTED,570,571,,"PR #567 established the deterministic ACTIVE-unit Phase-2 production/labor/INPUT planner and canonical INPUT budget commitments. PR #571 completes the repaired REQ-PRODUCTION-002 boundary from HANDOFF-REPAIR-M4-004 / Handoff/05 sections 19-20: ordinary investment review runs only on tick > 0 cadence multiples; demand, margin and sales pressure use the fixed equal one-third weights; workingCapitalTarget protects mandatoryKnownCash + grossWageCashEnvelope + desiredInputCost + operatingLiquidityBuffer before investment; investmentBudget is bounded from excess opening home cash; desired capital growth is capped by maxCapitalGrowthPerReview; existing INVESTMENT inventory is subtracted; material desired purchases require finite positive prior-close gross INVESTMENT prices; goods and IDs are stable-good ordered; canonical BUY/INVESTMENT intents keep sourcePlanId=ProductionPlan.planId, inventoryBucket=INVESTMENT and commit maxSpend through a distinct `${planId}:INVESTMENT` budget-ledger envelope. Focused regressions in src/simulation/productionPlanning.test.ts prove due-cadence pressure/budget/intents, genesis/off-cadence suppression, price-evidence fail-fast, distinct INPUT versus INVESTMENT commitments with duplicate-overcommit rejection, insertion-order determinism, same-tick transaction/market context non-financing, and no planning-time installedCapital or investmentInventory mutation. Phase-3 labor allocation, Phase-5 execution/output sale, Phase-12 capital formation/depreciation, lifecycle transitions, MOTHBALLED reactivation eligibility and M5+ remain owned by their separate requirements and are not claimed here."
